WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.010
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse has finally
arrived in theaters, giving everyone a chance

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.680
to dig into one of the most anticipated movies
of the year.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:12.200
The movie is also fairly complex, blending
a massive cast of characters with different

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.100
animation styles, multiple villains, and a
plot line that hops dimensions.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.119
If you're still trying to figure it all out,
we're here to help.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.950
Oh, and that weird feeling?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.660
That's your spoiler sense tingling.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:24.880
"Hey guys."

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.080
"Wanda?"

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.760
"Gwen, actually."

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.860
"Oh, you know her.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.020
Very cool."

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.580
From the moment she's revealed as in the film,
Gwen Stacy makes it clear that she's not interested

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.620
in making friends.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.470
Of course, that changes over the course of
the film, and by the end she's definitely

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.620
interested in a friendship with Miles Morales.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.830
Luckily, these spider pals have figured out
a way to stay in touch across dimensions,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.100
when she seems to visit him right before the
credits roll.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.560
The film doesn't take the time at the end
to explain why or how this is actually happening,

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.600
but it's an obvious setup for a Spider-gang
in the inevitable sequel.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.440
Miles Morales learns throughout the film that
he can't just be Spider-Man in some kind of

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.600
magic, automatic way.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.260
He has to take the leap of faith and become
Spider-Man in a way that's true to him.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.180
We see this in a thrilling sequence in which
he creates his own Spider-suit and heads out

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.000
into the world with his own unique threads.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:17.060
In the final moments of the film, we see that
he's continued his street art tradition both

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.680
as Miles and as Spider-Man.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:24.420
In the end, Miles carries on the long tradition
of refusing to kill his nemesis, and instead

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.400
turns Kingpin over to the authorities.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:31.310
We know two things about this universe's Kingpin
for sure: He has considerable resources, and

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:34.660
he is absolutely relentless in his pursuit
of getting what he wants.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:39.420
Chances are that what he wants most after
the credits is vengeance upon the new Spider-Man.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.900
Don't be surprised if he manages to show up
in some fashion in a sequel.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.580
Into the Spider-Verse is largely Miles' story,
but he's not the only Spider-Man to learn

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.080
a lesson.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:54.260
In teaching Miles how to use his powers, Peter
B. Parker also re-learns the lessons of great

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.130
power and great responsibility that he had
to internalize all those years ago.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.480
"We're a little team!

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.460
Me as the teacher who can still do it.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.360
You as the student who can do it but not as
well.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.880
I'm proud of us!"

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.920
When we first meet him, he's a Spider-Man
on auto-pilot, shrugging his way through crime-fighting

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:13.340
while his personal life is in shambles.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:17.140
In meeting Miles, he finds an opportunity
to teach and to learn about what it is to

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.500
be a hero all over again.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.250
By the time he returns to his home universe,
he's a changed man.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.840
Not just an Amazing Spider-Man, but an amazing
man.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.170
A couple of months before Into the Spider-Verse
hit theaters, Sony released another film based

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.060
on a Marvel Comics character with a very close
Spider-Man connection: Venom.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.540
That film included two post-credits scenes,
one of which seemed to be just an extended

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:42.660
clip to promote Into the Spider-Verse, which
included an important title card telling us

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.200
that the upcoming animated film was taking
place "In another universe."

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.689
Does this mean that Tom Hardy's Venom could
show up in future installments of the Spider-Verse

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:51.180
franchise?

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.020
"I HAVE PROOF!”

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.280
The answer is a definite...maybe.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.240
But that would be a truly wild crossover indeed.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.260
Miles' father Jefferson is a police officer
who views Spider-Man as a menace — until,

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.780
that is, he sees the new Spider-Man in action
at the end of the film.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.090
His very vocal change of heart during the
final battle helps Miles to defeat Kingpin,

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.680
and Miles returns the favor by finally telling
his dad he loves him — well, sort of.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.020
"Officer, I love you."

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.540
"haha, wait, what?"

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:27.360
It's a big emotional payoff in the film, giving
Miles the opportunity to covertly tell his

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.580
father what he's been holding back.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.980
It might also be the new Spider-Man accidently
hinting at his identity.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.900
If that's the case, it might not be long before
Miles is outed as Spider-Man to his parents.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:43.459
In the end, Miles Morales is able to send
all of his friends back home and defeat Kingpin.

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:47.749
Still, this is a superhero universe with a
sequel on the way, so we know his version

00:03:47.749 --> 00:03:49.680
of New York City won't stay quiet for long.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.700
So who will Miles fight the next time around?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.939
The clear contender could be the Green Goblin,
who shows up in this film for its first major

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.780
fight scene but is ultimately relegated to
a minor role.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.480
We're betting the Green Goblin, and his alter
ego Norman Osborn, could have a much larger

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.800
role to play in the sequel.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.000
The film's post-credits scene reveals yet
another Spider-hero, as we see a costumed

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.709
figure named Miguel jump into the past and
get in an argument with the Spider-Man from

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:16.420
the 1967 animated series.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.900
The Miguel in question is Miguel O'Hara, a.k.a.
Spider-Man 2099.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.220
In the comics and in the film, he has the
ability to hop through dimensions, which means

00:04:25.229 --> 00:04:29.680
he could show up alongside any of Into the
Spider-Verse's heroes at a moment's notice.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.200
Keep an eye out for him in the follow-up.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.640
Of course, we all know who we really want
to come back next time we visit the Spider-Verse:

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.820
"I just washed my hands, that's why they're
wet.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:40.940
No other reason."

